{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he shall give to the priest the holy thing.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory disagreed in chapter 6 of Tractate Terumot: Rabbi Eliezer says — anything fit to become holy; and Rabbi Akiva says — the holy thing that he ate. End of quote. And perhaps it intends to say that through this act of giving, Scripture credits him as though he gave the holy thing itself, and as though he had not eaten the holy thing."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:00:14.738711592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}